# 9. Vulnerability Scanner Report Mental Model

When analysing a vulnerability scanner finding, use the following structure:

```text
WHAT?
↓
What vulnerability was detected?

WHERE?
↓
Which host/port is affected?

HOW SERIOUS?
↓
What severity/risk information is reported?

WHY?
↓
Why does the finding matter?

HOW TO FIX?
↓
What remediation is recommended?
```

This approach is useful when reviewing vulnerability assessment reports during penetration testing or defensive security assessments.

