# Final Learning Summary

This module introduced the defensive side of cybersecurity.

The major concepts can be connected as follows:

```text
                 SECURITY OPERATIONS
                         │
        ┌────────────────┼────────────────┐
        │                │                │
       SIEM           Network           Vulnerability
        │              Security          Assessment
        │                │                │
     Logs          Firewall / IDS      OpenVAS
        │                │                │
   Correlation           │             Findings
        │                │                │
      Alerts          IPS            Remediation
        │
  Investigation
```

The key distinction between the major technologies is:

```text
SIEM
→ Collects and correlates security events

Firewall
→ Controls network traffic

IDS
→ Detects suspicious activity and alerts

IPS
→ Detects and can prevent/block suspicious traffic

Vulnerability Scanner
→ Identifies known weaknesses

OpenVAS
→ Performs vulnerability assessment and reporting

Snort
→ Analyses network traffic using detection rules
```

Together, these technologies demonstrate an important defensive-security workflow:

```text
Collect
  ↓
Monitor
  ↓
Detect
  ↓
Alert
  ↓
Investigate
  ↓
Identify Weaknesses
  ↓
Remediate
```

This module therefore provides a foundation for understanding how security teams monitor environments, detect suspicious activity, assess vulnerabilities, and respond to security findings.
